The BCM2837 target cannot link: the Blocks runtime is never built.

xnu uses blocks (^{ }) in IOKit, libkern and the scheduler -- OSSerializer::
withBlock, IOService::registerInterest, IOMemoryDescriptor::makeMapping,
turnstile.c, waitq.c -- so the kernel needs the runtime that backs them. In
xnu that runtime is libkern/libclosure, and libkern/conf/files builds it only
when the config option is set:

    libkern/libclosure/runtime.cpp      optional config_blocks
    libkern/libclosure/libclosuredata.c optional config_blocks

config/MASTER.arm64.bcm2837 does not set it. Both files are skipped and the
link ends with:

    "__Block_object_assign", referenced from: ...
    "__Block_object_dispose", referenced from: ...
    "__Block_release", referenced from: ...
    "__NSConcreteGlobalBlock", referenced from: ...
    "__NSConcreteStackBlock", referenced from: ...
    ld: symbol(s) not found for architecture arm64

This is an omission, not a decision. MASTER.arm64, MASTER.arm and
MASTER.x86_64 all carry config_blocks in LIBKERN_BASE; the BCM2837 file was
last touched in 2016 and never picked it up, along with several other
options the 2018 configs gained. Apple shipped this config for the public
source release and never linked it, so the gap went unnoticed.

Add the option. Nothing else is needed: runtime.cpp defines _Block_copy,
_Block_release, _Block_object_assign and _Block_object_dispose, and
libclosuredata.c defines the _NSConcrete*Block class placeholders -- the
whole set the linker is asking for.

Deliberately not added here: config_img4 (the other LIBKERN_BASE entry this
file is missing). Image4 is Apple's signed-boot-manifest validation; a
non-Apple board has no use for it and config_enforce_signed_code is off on
this target too.

--- a/config/MASTER.arm64.bcm2837
+++ b/config/MASTER.arm64.bcm2837
@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@
 #  IOKIT_RELEASE =  [ IOKIT_BASE ]
 #  IOKIT_DEV =      [ IOKIT_BASE iokitstats iotracking ]
 #  IOKIT_DEBUG =    [ IOKIT_BASE iokitstats iotracking]
-#  LIBKERN_BASE =   [ libkerncpp config_kec_fips zlib crypto_sha2 ]
+#  LIBKERN_BASE =   [ libkerncpp config_blocks config_kec_fips zlib crypto_sha2 ]
 #  LIBKERN_RELEASE =[ LIBKERN_BASE ]
 #  LIBKERN_DEV =    [ LIBKERN_BASE iotracking ]
 #  LIBKERN_DEBUG =  [ LIBKERN_BASE iotracking ]
